# Friendly path → canonical subdomain redirects, served by the landing Worker's
# static-assets layer (same mechanism as _headers). Each property lives on its
# own subdomain; these paths are conveniences that send visitors (and link
# equity) to the canonical host. 301 = permanent: the subdomain IS the home.
#
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>. The bare path redirects to the
# subdomain root; the /* rule preserves any sub-path via :splat, so deep links
# survive (noeta.dev/docs/reactivity → docs.noeta.dev/reactivity). First match
# wins, so the exact path precedes its wildcard.

/docs             https://docs.noeta.dev/          301
/docs/*           https://docs.noeta.dev/:splat    301

/playground       https://play.noeta.dev/          301
/playground/*     https://play.noeta.dev/:splat    301

/registry         https://registry.noeta.dev/      301
/registry/*       https://registry.noeta.dev/:splat 301

# The one-line installer: `curl -fsSL https://noeta.dev/install | sh`. 302, not 301 —
# the script's canonical home (raw GitHub today) is an implementation detail that may move.
/install          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/noeta-lang/noeta/main/install.sh 302
